: Statement ]\nL323: \nL324: [Button: Hide Toolbar ]\nL325: \nL326: Back\nL327: ## Accessibility Commitment for Carolyn's Pumpkin Patch\nL328: \nL329: At Carolyn's Pumpkin Patch, we are committed to making our digital presence as accessible and inclusive as reasonably possible for all users, including individuals with disabilities. Our goal is to improve the usability of carolynspumpkinpatch.com and to support a more accessible experience for everyone, regardless of their abilities or the technologies they use.\nL330: ### Our Approach to Accessibility\nL331: \nL332: We aim to align with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG), which define internationally recognized standards for digital accessibility. While full compliance cannot always be guaranteed, we strive to implement improvements where feasible and regularly review accessibility-related aspects of our website. Accessibility is an ongoing process, and we are committed to improving the experience over time as technologies, standards, and user needs evolve.\nL333: ### Accessibility Features\nL334: \nL335: To support accessibility, carolynspumpkinpatch.com may utilize tools such as the OneTap accessibility toolbar. This interface provides users with a range of helpful features, including:\nL336: \nL337:   * Adjustable text size and contrast settings\nL338:   * Highlighting of links and text for better visibility\nL339:   * Full keyboard navigation of the toolbar interface\nL340:   * Quick launch via keyboard shortcut: Alt + . (Windows) or ⌘ + . (Mac)\nL341: Please note the following:\nL342:   * The availability and effectiveness of these features depend on the website's configuration and ongoing maintenance.\nL343:   * While we strive to ensure accessibility, we cannot guarantee that every part of carolynspumpkinpatch.com will be fully accessible at all times. Some content may be provided by third parties or affected by technical constraints beyond our immediate control.\nL344: ### Feedback and Contact\nL345: \nL346: We welcome your feedback. If you experience any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement, please contact us: Email: info@carolynspumpkinpatch.com We are committed to reviewing all inquiries and aim to respond within 3–5 business days. If you require assistance accessing any part of this website, we are happy to provide support through alternative channels upon request. Last updated: November 14, 2025\nL347: \nL348: How long do you want to hide the toolbar?\nL349: Hide Toolbar Duration [Input] Only for this session [Input] 24 hours [Input] A Week\nL350: \nL351: [Button: Not Now] [Button: Hide Toolbar]\nL352: \nL353: Select your accessibility profile\nL354: \nL355: Vision Impaired Mode\nL356: \nL357: Enhances website's visuals\nL358: \nL359: [Input] Vision Impaired Mode\nL360: \nL361: Seizure Safe Profile\nL362: \nL363: Clear flashes & reduces color\nL364: \nL365: [Input] Seizure Safe Profile\nL366: \nL367: ADHD Friendly Mode\nL368: \nL369: Focused browsing, distraction-free\nL370: \nL371: [Input] ADHD Friendly Mode\nL372: \nL373: Blindness Mode\nL374: \nL375: Reduces distractions, improves focus\nL376: \nL377: [Input] Blindness Mode\nL378: \nL379: Epilepsy Safe Mode\nL380: Dims colors and stops blinking\nL381: \nL382: [Input] Epilepsy Safe Mode\nL383: \nL384: Content Modules\nL385: \nL386: Font Size\nL387: \nL388: Default\nL389: \nL390: Highlight Links\nL391: \nL392: Line Height\nL393: \nL394: Default\nL395: \nL396: Readable Font\nL397: \nL398: Cursor\nL399: \nL400: Text Magnifier\nL401: \nL402: Dyslexic Font\nL403: \nL404: Align Text\nL405: \nL406: Letter Spacing\nL407: \nL408: Font Weight\nL409: \nL410: Color Modules\nL411: \nL412: Dark Contrast\nL413: \nL414: Light Contrast\nL415: \nL416: High Contrast\nL417: \nL418: Monochrome\nL419: \nL420: Saturation\nL421: \nL422: Orientation Modules\nL423: \nL424: Reading Line\nL425: \nL426: Reading Mask\nL427: Browser needs to be updated Your browser doesn’t support speech output. Please update your browser or use one with speech synthesis enabled (e.g. Chrome, Edge, Safari). cite39†How to Update? L428: \nL429: Read Page\nL430: \nL431: Keyboard Navigation\nL432: \nL433: Hide Images\nL434: \nL435: Mute Sounds\nL436: \nL437: Highlight Titles\nL438: \nL439: Highlight Content\nL440: \nL441: Stop Animations\nL442: \nL443: Skip To Content [Select]\nL444: \nL445: [Button: Reset Settings ]\nL446: \nL447:   * cite83†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTerror On Route 66 | Haunted House | Sullivan, Missouri (https://scarestl.com/)\nciteturn305view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://scarestl.com/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 117\nL0: cite0†Image: Terror On Route 66 Haunted House L1: \nL2: Missouri's Most EXTREME Haunted Attraction!\nL3: \nL4: cite1†HOME cite2†BUY TICKETS cite3†WARNING! cite4†SCHEDULE cite5†DIRECTIONS cite6†JOBS cite7†VENDORS cite8†CONTACT L5: \nL6: cite9†Terror On Route 66†www.youtube.com [Button: 🔇 ]\nL7: \nL8: ## BUY TICKETS\nL9: \nL10: ### Welcome to Terror On Route 66 Haunted House!\nL11: \nL12: ALL PARTICIPANTS ARE REQUIRED TO FILL OUT A WAIVER BEFORE ENTERING THE ATTRACTION!\nL13: \nL14: Open rain or shine unless posted otherwise on our Facebook page!\nL15: ### General Admission\nL16: \nL17: General Admission is your traditional haunted house walk through with jump scares and skits. No touch involved.\nL18: \nL19: ### Fast Pass\nL20: \nL21: Skip the general admission line, shorter wait time.\nL22: \nL23: ### Interactive Touch Pass\nL24: \nL25: Ages 10+. All minors under the age of 18 MUST BE ACCOMPANIED WITH AN ADULT with a valid ID! Interactive Touch Pass is kid friendly and includes light touching such as messing with hair, head, ears, arms and neck. No inappropriate or harmful touching.\nL26: ### RATED R Pass\nL27: \nL28: 18+ ONLY. WARNING: DARK HUMOR, ADULT LANGUAGE and INTENSE CONTACT. Rated R Pass is our most intense admission option. This is a FULL contact touch experience. Includes safe intense full contact, adult language and dark humor. No inappropriate or harmful touching. IF YOU ARE SENSITIVE OR EASILY OFFENDED THIS UPGRADE IS NOT RECOMMENDED. Rated R Pass participants cannot enter the attraction in a group with guests who do not have Rated R Passes.\nL29: ### Terror Pass\nL30: \nL31: Includes: Fast Pass + Choice of Interactive Touch Pass or Rated R Pass.\nL32: ### VIP Terror Pass\nL33: \nL34: Includes: Front of Line + Choice of Interactive Touch Pass or Rated R Pass + VIP gift + VIP Lanyard.\nL35: \nL36: A Valid ID must be presented at check-in for all INTERACTIVE TOUCH PASS and RATED R PASS participants.\nL37: \nL38: Rated R Pass participants cannot enter the attraction in a group with guests who do not have Rated R Passes. General Admission and Touch Pass guests may go together. Detailed ticket descriptions above.\nL39: \nL40: All sales are final! No refunds. No exceptions. Open Rain or Shine!\nL41: Tickets are valid any open night during our 2026 Halloween Season ending Nov 1!\nL42: \nL43: cite10†BUY TICKETS NOW†www.simpletix.com L44: ## WARNING!\nL45: ### ENTER AT YOUR OWN RISK\nL46:   * All participants must complete a waiver before entering the attraction.\nL47:   * Interactive Touch Pass participants must be age 10 or older.\nL48:   * Minors under 18 must be accompanied by an adult with valid ID for Interactive Touch Pass.\nL49:   * Rated R Pass is strictly for guests age 18+.\nL50:   * Valid ID is required at check-in for Interactive Touch Pass and Rated R Pass participants.\nL51:   * Rated R participants cannot enter in a group with guests who do not have Rated R Passes.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHOME | FoS Branson (https://www.fieldofscreamsbranson.com/home-1)\nciteturn305view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.fieldofscreamsbranson.com/home-1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 92\n"
